# THE Foundry toolchain both CI workflows resolve. Requirement CI-05.
#
# This file exists so that changing what CI compiles with is a REVIEWABLE DIFF. The
# self-hosted `cfmm-build` runner is persistent: anyone running `foundryup` on that box
# silently changes what every future run measures, with no commit, no PR and no trace. A
# version literal living only inside workflow YAML would also let the push workflow and the
# PR gate drift apart. Both workflows source THIS file, so there is exactly one pin and
# moving it costs a commit.
#
# WHY THIS VERSION -- and what breaks if it moves: notes/TOOLCHAIN_PINS.md.
#
# Format: shell-sourceable KEY=value. Consumed by
#   .github/workflows/push-build.yml    (unattended push build)
#   .github/workflows/develop-gate.yml  (the PR/merge gate, forge job)
# via `. ./.github/foundry-version`. Keep it sourceable: no spaces around `=`, no command
# substitution, comments only on their own lines.

# The release tag. Passed to `foundryup --install "${FOUNDRY_VERSION#v}"`.
FOUNDRY_VERSION=v1.5.1

# The commit the pinned release was built from. THIS is the assertion the workflows make --
# a tag can in principle be re-cut, and "1.5.1" alone would not notice. `forge --version`
# prints this SHA, so a run either matches it or goes red.
FOUNDRY_COMMIT=b0a9dd9ceda36f63e2326ce530c10e6916f4b8a2

# The foundryup INSTALLER is pinned too: an unpinned installer is an unpinned supply chain
# for the pinned toolchain. This is the same commit foundry-rs/foundry-toolchain@v1 pins in
# its own src/index.ts (FOUNDRYUP_INSTALLER_COMMIT).
FOUNDRYUP_INSTALLER_COMMIT=a27902ef04dcb43061fabf343365cb5afc95fc48
